# conformance vectors are Rust-generated canonical bytes (M22.4) — byte-compared against regeneration
conformance/

# The shared policy artifacts (M24.1) are byte-checked: every digest-pinned
# file here, policy.v3.json and tools.v1.json included, is hashed against its
# committed .sha256 by the loaders that read it, and every authority-routes
# snapshot IS the canonical bytes its filename hashes. A formatter that
# reflowed one would break the anchor that proves every loader read the same
# rules.
shared/policy/

# The shipped budget ceilings (M25.2) are compiled in and hashed against a
# committed digest, for the same reason: a reflow would change the bytes and
# therefore change what tomorrow costs, silently.
shared/runtime/

# The model reads shared/prompt/ byte for byte from Rust and TS (M54.7): a reflow would change what every run is told.
shared/prompt/

# The field-kind table and the date grammar (M60.3) are hashed against their
# committed .sha256 by Rust (include_str!) and by vitest: a reflow would change
# the bytes both readers must agree on.
shared/schema/
shared/calendar/

# The file-kind table (M66.1) is hashed against its committed .sha256 by Rust
# (include_str!) and by vitest, and keeps one row per line: a reflow would
# change the bytes both readers must agree on.
shared/files/

# JSON Canvas format and round-trip goldens are byte anchors (M68.2).
shared/canvas/

# Starter files install byte for byte in Rust and the browser mock.
shared/starter/

# Shared import artifact bytes are deliberate and hashed.
shared/import/

